    "title": "Step Inside This Historic Texas Bowling Club Where They Still Set The Nine Pins By Hand - NewsBreak",
    "text": "13 hours ago There is a small town just outside San Antonio where bowling looks nothing like the neon lanes most people know. No automatic machines sweep away the pins here. Instead, a person crouches at the end of the lane and resets everything by hand, keeping a German tradition alive that has nearly faded from Texas altogether. The game uses nine pins, not ten, and it plays out as a genuine team sport rather than a solo score chase. Read full article",
